It's why the OP had such a good question.

Consider how good a unihorn is as a weapon, and then
consider that isn't even its primary function.  It
must do something awesome for its primary function.

Consider how bad a worm tooth is as a weapon, and
then consider that it has secondary functions.  If
must suck at those secondary functions.  View that
worm tooth as a tin opener and it does suck at it.
View that worm tooth as the larval form of a
crysknife, and it sucks in comparison.

Weapons go through a wide range of qualities.  Worm
tooth is down near rubber hose near the bottom of
the list.  Tools go through a wide range of qualities.
Unihorn is very high in that list.

Weapons and tools that function as both do have some
correlation as to how good they are.  Daggers may
be wonderfull as missiles, but there are very many
better melee weapons.  Sure enough they do poorly
as tin openers.  Bull whip is a poor weapon and only
rarely usefull as a tool.  Pick axe is near the
middle among weaon qualities and as a tool it is
near the middle on usefullness.  The pattern is not
exact and it is open to interpretation, but the
pattern is there.



